SPARK TOUR

Windows: run Launch Tour.exe. A local browser and control tab open. Stop the server from its control tab or close the launcher console.

Local network / Quest: in the launcher control tab, choose Share on this network. Scan the QR or enter the HTTPS address on a device on the same network. A self-signed certificate warning appears on first use; verify the address against the launcher before continuing. Allow the launcher through Windows Firewall on private networks if needed. Stop sharing from the control tab.

Hosting: upload this folder to a static HTTPS host (the EXE is only for local Windows viewing). Preserve subdirectories. Serve .rad with HTTP Range / 206 responses. Configure CORS on a remote asset host.

Edit config/hosting.json to change assetBaseUrl (relative or HTTPS, ending with /) or sceneUrls overrides. These settings affect splats, not the application.

Reopen this folder in Spark Tour Studio to edit the tour. Runtime code is bundled locally. External links/custom pages may still depend on online services.

Export mode: referenced assets
